{
  "name": "Ember-Touched Greatsword",
  "type": "weapon",
  "img": "modules/dnd-players-handbook/assets/icons/items/greatsword.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Weapon (Greatsword), Common</em></p><p>A staple of the Flaming Fist of Baldur's Gate — duty-blades quenched, their smiths swear, in the company's own forge-fire, so the steel keeps a banked heat that never quite goes out. The pawnbroker on Daggerford's market square sold it cheap; he was tired, he said, of his shop window smoldering like a hearth after dark.</p><p>In Darkness, the unsheathed blade of this weapon glows like charcoal embers, creating Bright Light in a 15-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 15 feet.</p><p>The banked heat sears where the blade bites: when you hit with an attack roll using this magic weapon, the target takes an extra 1 Fire damage.</p>",
